{
  "_comment": [
    "Every third-party file the playground ships, pinned by SHA-256.",
    "",
    "The app has no package manager: its dependencies are committed blobs, some",
    "of them minified megabytes that no reviewer reads. Two things follow. A",
    "change to one is invisible in a pull request, so the hashes here are what",
    "makes an edit to vendored code a deliberate, reviewable act rather than a",
    "line in a diff nobody opens. And nothing else records what these files ARE,",
    "so `version` is what makes it possible to ask whether a shipped library has",
    "a published advisory against it.",
    "",
    "To update one: replace the file, run `node scripts/check_vendor_integrity.mjs",
    "--update`, and record the new version in the same commit.",
    "",
    "`version: null` means the build carries no version string. Pin it by hash,",
    "and record the version here when the file is next replaced from a known",
    "release."
  ],
